course: dictionary
lesson: 9727
title: Plants that eat insects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sundew is a small plant that eats insects. Most plants make their own food from sunlight, but this one grows in boggy ground where the soil is poor in nitrogen, a nutrient plants need. «Bog soil has very little nitrogen, so the sundew catches insects on sticky drops.» It gets the extra nitrogen it lacks from its prey.
explain: Look at the clues in that sentence. The sticky drops catch the insects, and then the plant digests them. Digest means breaks down food so the body can use it. It is what your stomach does to your dinner.
explain: «A sundew's leaves have red hairs tipped with sticky drops that glitter like dew.» Glitter means shine, and dew is the water drops you see on grass in the morning. The leaves look pretty, but they are a trap: when an insect is stuck, the hairs slowly bend over it.
explain: A plant that eats animals is called carnivorous, which means meat-eating. A sundew is one example, and the Venus flytrap is another. Both are carnivorous plants.
fact: A sundew is a small meat-eating plant that grows in boggy places.
fact: Its leaves are covered in sticky, shining hairs that trap insects.
fact: The hairs bend over the insect, and the plant digests it.
fact: «Carnivorous» means meat-eating, and a sundew is a carnivorous plant.
fact: Bog soil is poor in nitrogen, so the sundew gets extra food from the insects it catches.
exercise: What kind of plant is a sundew? | A water plant that grows in rivers | *A small meat-eating plant that traps insects | A flower that only opens at night | A tall tree with thick bark
exercise: «A sundew's leaves have sticky drops that glitter like dew.» What does glitter mean here? | Turn brown | Drip slowly | Fall off | *Shine
exercise: Why does a sundew catch insects? | To keep its roots warm | To scare away birds | To grow taller in the sun | *Because bog soil has very little nitrogen
test: Which word means meat-eating? | Woody | Herbivorous | *Carnivorous | Aquatic
test: What does a sundew do to the insects it traps? | Gives them water to drink | Hides them under the soil | Lets them go free | *Digests them to get nitrogen
exam: Name another plant that catches insects, like the sundew. | Oak | Rose | Dandelion | *Venus flytrap
